4	// On a project's detail page each invoice shows its status (invoice-status) and, once it has been
5	// SENT, offers a control to mark it paid (invoice-pay-<id>). Marking an invoice paid flips THAT
6	// invoice's status to paid and appends one audit record — INVOICE_PAID id=<id> amount=<amount> — so
7	// the action can be checked back later. Marking one invoice must not touch its siblings, and each
8	// marking writes its own record ("every time I do").
9	//
10	// Invoices now move through stages (DRAFT -> SENT -> PAID) and payment is only allowed once an
11	// invoice has been sent (see invoice-send.spec.ts). So these tests seed invoices already at the SENT
12	// stage (status: 'SENT') — the point where they are payable — and drive the pay flow from there.
13	//
